      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 415: 🔴 `event.target.setPointerCapture(...)` captures the pointer on the handle element, but move/up/cancel listeners are registered on `document`. Once capture is active, subsequent pointer events are retargeted to the handle, so the document listeners may not receive `pointermove`/`pointerup`; the drag can get stuck and leave a local-only width until cancellation. Register the move/up/cancel listeners on the captured handle, or avoid pointer capture when listening on `document`.",
